Data from a physical test
A test is useful for judging a simulator when its setup can be rebuilt. A submission contains:

the measured quantities, as numbers, in SI or with their units stated;
the soil: what it is, its grain size, and its density in the test;
the bed: container size, fill depth, and how the soil was placed;
the tool or vehicle: shape, size, mass where it matters;
the motion: how the tool moved or was loaded, and how fast;
what was measured, with which instrument, and anything known about its accuracy;
what is not known, said plainly;
the source (a report, a paper, or the laboratory that ran the test) and permission to share the data.

A script that runs a virtual experiment
A virtual experiment script mirrors one of the tests hosted here in a simulator. A submission states:

which test it mirrors (the record id on the test’s page);
the simulator and its version;
the inputs chosen where the record is silent (the choices left to the user on the test’s card), with the reason for each;
its output, in the quantity that was measured (for a load-penetration test, the load on the tool against its penetration).
